  "body": "## What changed\n\n- `assets/posts/fanuc.cps` and `assets/posts/doosan-dnm.cps`: a new flag `tcpmLeft`. `endPreamble` copies `tcpmOn` into it before the reset.\n- `onClose` in the two posts writes `G49` before its own retract when `tcpmLeft` is true.\n- `crates/post/tests/recorded/golden/fanuc/rotary.nc`: one new `G49` line after `M5`.\n- Two new pins in `crates/post/tests/upright_after_tilt/program_end.rs` (no new test binary).\n- Decision record: `docs/decisions/4348-g49-before-end-home.md`.\n\n## Cause\n\n`tilt()` arms `G43.4 H<n>`. A section that tilts and then stands upright again ends with no rotary off zero. Then `uprightAtEnd()` writes nothing. `endPreamble` sets `tcpmOn = false` and writes no `G49`, because the next preamble writes `G49`. At the program end there is no next preamble. So `onClose` wrote `G91 G28 Z0` and `G28 X0 Y0` under `G43.4`. The FANUC 30i manual (B-63944EN/02) does not permit a reference return in `G43.4` mode.\n\nThe other exits are unchanged. They already write `G49`: a held rotary (`uprightAtEnd()`), a trailing Go home (`afterOp`), and the next preamble.\n\n## Tests\n\nPins (binary `upright_after_tilt`):\n- `program_end::fanuc_cancels_tcpm_before_program_end_after_a_tilt_back_to_zero` (G28 and G53 retract modes)\n- `program_end::doosan_cancels_tcpm_before_program_end_after_a_tilt_back_to_zero` (G28 and G53 retract modes)\n\nEach pin asserts a `G49` between the last `G43.4` and the end retract. In G28 mode it also asserts the exact tail: `M5`, `G49`, `G91 G28 Z0`, `G28 X0 Y0`, `M30`, `%`.\n\nThe recorded golden `script_fanuc` `rotary` also pins the order now.\n\nRed before the fix: yes. Both pins failed on unchanged `a721fd4dc` with \"G49 cancels G43.4 before the end retract\". The program showed `M5` then `G91 G28 Z0`.\n\nMutation checks (old post put back with `git checkout upstream/main -- <post>`, then restored):\n- old `fanuc.cps`: the Fanuc pin is red, the Doosan pin is green.\n- old `doosan-dnm.cps`: the Doosan pin is red, the Fanuc pin is green.\n- restored: the two pins are green. The `upright_after_tilt` binary passes 19 of 19.\n\nGate on the final head `23972c2d8` (base `a721fd4dc`):\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: 148 steps. The first run had one red step, `post suites: script_fanuc` (`rotary`), because the recorded golden recorded the defect. I updated the golden (one `G49` line). Then `--only \"post suites: script_fanuc\"` passed 11 of 11. The other 147 steps were green, including `app suites: example_catalog`, `example_catalog_adaptive`, `example_catalog_edge_work`, `conformance`, `doosan_dnm_post`, `fanuc_post` and `setup_change`.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-post --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- `cargo xtask gate heavy --base upstream/main` on `23972c2d8`: 7 steps, 0 failed (release build, and the app heavy steps `do_not_touch`, `do_not_touch_adaptive`, `lathe_workholding_kinds`, `mcp`, `probe_no_coolant`, `sinker_burn`).\n- `cargo xtask gate light` on `23972c2d8`: 6 steps, 0 failed.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nOne: `crates/post/tests/recorded/golden/fanuc/rotary.nc`. It is a tilted section that ends at `A0 B0`. It gains one `G49` line after `M5`, before `G91 G28 Z0`. No other line changed. The example catalog suites and the app `nc/` goldens (`conformance`) did not move: their programs end through a path that already writes `G49`, or never arm `G43.4`.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No run on a real FANUC or Doosan control.\n- The Fanuc setup-change path (`afterOp` with a next setup and a stop ask) also writes `G91 G28 Z0` under `G43.4`. The Doosan post already writes `G49` there (#1647). This is outside the scope of #4348, and this PR does not change it. It needs a follow-up issue.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nNo open PR changes `assets/posts/fanuc.cps` or `assets/posts/doosan-dnm.cps`. Upstream `main` moved to `79f4dbe4a` after the base. The new commits do not touch `assets/posts` or `crates/post`.\n\nEffort: high\n\nChangelog: Fanuc and Doosan DNM posts: a program whose last tilted section ends at zero angles now writes G49 before the program-end reference return, so G43.4 is not active at G28.\n\nFixes #4348\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
